Day 6 — Real-time (Socket.io) + Frontend Integration

GOAL: Wire Socket.io so order status changes push live to the browser, build the
delivery module, then scaffold + build the full Next.js frontend.

Architecture recap: Socket.io shares the HTTP server from server.ts. The Redis adapter
(Pub/Sub) lets real-time work across multiple Node instances. When notification.worker
receives a status-changed job, it emits a Socket.io event to room "order:{orderId}".
The connected browser gets the update instantly — no polling, no refresh.

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Piece 1 — Socket.io backend (realtime/)

- npm i socket.io @socket.io/redis-adapter
- realtime/socket.events.ts — event name constants (ORDER_STATUS_UPDATED,
  DELIVERY_LOCATION_UPDATED, ORDER_NEW). No hardcoded strings.
- realtime/socket.auth.ts — middleware that verifies JWT on WebSocket handshake.
  Same verifyToken() used by HTTP auth.middleware, but adapted for Socket.io's
  handshake flow (socket.handshake.auth.token).
- realtime/handlers/order.handler.ts — client joins room `order:{orderId}` to
  receive status updates for that order. Also handles restaurant owners joining
  `restaurant:{id}` to get all new orders for their restaurant.
- realtime/handlers/delivery.handler.ts — delivery partner pushes location
  updates; server broadcasts to room `order:{orderId}` so customer sees movement.
- realtime/socket.ts — creates the Socket.io server, attaches Redis adapter for
  Pub/Sub, registers the auth middleware, wires handlers. Exports `io` and
  `initSocket(httpServer)`.

Update server.ts — call initSocket(server) after app.listen.

Piece 2 — Delivery module (modules/delivery/)

- delivery.types.ts — DeliveryAssignmentRow, validators.
- delivery.service.ts — assignPartner(orderId, partnerId), updateStatus,
  updateLocation, getAssignment.
- delivery.controller.ts, delivery.routes.ts — DELIVERY role only for
  updates/location; customer/owner can view. Mount /api/delivery in app.ts.

Piece 3 — Update notification.worker.ts

- Import io from realtime/socket.ts.
- Actually emit ORDER_STATUS_UPDATED to room `order:{orderId}`.
- For restaurant owners, emit ORDER_NEW to `restaurant:{restaurantId}`.

